.TH ifg-agent 1  "ifg-agent 0.9.1"
.SH NAME
ifg\-agent \- Manage the agent accounts you own and their tokens
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBifg agent\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage the agent accounts you own and their tokens
.PP
An agent is an account that belongs to you, named `<your username>\-agent\-<name>`, for tools that act on your behalf. These commands need your own login: an agent\*(Aqs token cannot manage agents. Its commits and API writes are attributed to the agent, and the audit log records you as the person it acted for.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ifg\-agent\-list(1)
List your agents
.TP
ifg\-agent\-create(1)
Create an agent
.TP
ifg\-agent\-view(1)
Show one agent
.TP
ifg\-agent\-edit(1)
Change an agent\*(Aqs description or switch it on or off
.TP
ifg\-agent\-token(1)
Manage an agent\*(Aqs tokens
.TP
ifg\-agent\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.9.1
